    "knowledge_point": "Graphing a Transformed Reciprocal Function",
    "problem": "Which of the following is the graph of $y=\\frac{1}{2(x+1)}?$",
    "worked_solution": "To plot $y=\\frac{1}{2(x+1)},$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=\\frac{1}{x}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13831126/assets/a32495fcca947d01cf8d3218fc5cfc0cce083a34e6fb6b629d92ba9e47039a6e.png)\n\n- Translate it by $1$ unit to the left to get the graph of $y=\\frac{1}{x+1}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13831126/assets/049f9c306c007026bc72e5f00d925cf22d80d94049aa82e3c81d7fc7c289249f.png)\n\n- Then, stretch the result by a scale factor of $\\frac{1}{2}$ parallel to the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=\\frac{1}{2(x+1)}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13831126/assets/c52f568868328061237d43e4650180321ec4a40e886a62f4a678f0276afe821b.png)",
